From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:32:10 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] crash-guard

A game that took slot down while it loaded starts on the shelf next time. Detection is upstream's (v1.9.0 loading_mark.rs: a mark in SLOT_RUN, set when a cart goes in, cleared after 10 s of play, on the shelf or on a clean stop). Ours is what the player sees: the cart that crashed is selected on the shelf and the banner Last start failed says why. Upstream also moves the resume state aside (resume-refused-*) and unseats the cart, where our first guard kept both. The Config/starting.txt mark is gone. ADR 0084, ADR 0109.
---
